description: Non-negotiable constraints for meownow. Always apply.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Invariants

- The server is untrusted. It must never see plaintext content, filenames, MIME types, or previews. If an approach requires plaintext server-side, stop and flag it.
- All authorization is server-side. UI gating is convenience, never enforcement. A user without `can_upload` must be unable to write a byte to R2 even with a hand-crafted request.
- Membership is invite-only. There is no public signup and no numeric seat cap. An unused invite is the only way in. `/play` is not a member: notes stay in this browser and never go to Neon, R2, or the hub.
- No passwords. Passkeys plus a recovery phrase. Never add a fallback.
- Zero recurring cost. Stay inside free tiers. Flag anything that would exceed one before building it.

# Corrections

- Vercel Postgres is gone. Use Neon via `@neondatabase/serverless`. Never `@vercel/postgres`.
- Vercel Functions cannot hold WebSockets and cap bodies at 4.5 MB. Realtime lives in a Durable Object; blobs go straight to R2 via the Worker.
- Web Bluetooth cannot connect two browsers. "Local" means WebRTC resolving to LAN host candidates.
- Browsers cannot monitor the clipboard in the background. Never write code or copy implying automatic capture.
- `next-pwa` is unmaintained. Use Serwist.

Follow milestones in `docs/SPEC.md` §1.9 in order. Stop at each boundary. If the spec is wrong, say so; do not silently reinterpret it.
